stream
BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 738 Td
14 TL
(1\) The simplest call) Tj
T*
(  const x = Waves.wave\(40, 'classicSine'\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2\) Make it bigger \(amplitude\)) Tj
T*
(  const x = Waves.wave\(40, 'classicSine', null, { amplitude: 120 }\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3\) Animate it) Tj
T*
(  let t = 0;) Tj
T*
(  const x = Waves.wave\(40 + t, 'classicSine'\);) Tj
T*
(  t += 0.02;) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4\) Return both axes \(x and z\)) Tj
T*
(  const o = Waves.wave\(40, 'classicSine', null, { axis: 'xz', amplitude: 60 }\);) Tj
T*
(  // o = { x, z }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5\) Instance mode) Tj
T*
(  new p5\(function \(p\) {) Tj
T*
(    p.draw = function \(\) {) Tj
T*
(      const x = p.waves\(40, 'classicSine'\);) Tj
T*
(    };) Tj
T*
(  }\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
(CHOOSING WAVES) Tj
T*
(------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
(You can select a wave by: - wave name \(string\) - shape name \(string\) - index \(number\)) Tj
T*
(Matching is case-insensitive and spaces/hyphens are ignored.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Examples:) Tj
T*
(  Waves.wave\(20, 'classicSine'\);) Tj
T*
(  Waves.wave\(20, 'Classic Sine'\);) Tj
T*
(  Waves.wave\(20, 'ellipse'\);) Tj
T*
(  Waves.wave\(20, 0\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Tip: If you want to avoid breaking changes in saved projects, store the wave string, not the) Tj
T*
(index.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
(WORKFLOW 1: SIMPLE LINE) Tj
T*
(------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
(Use the wave output as an X offset for a vertical line:) Tj
T*
(  for \(let y = 0; y < height; y += 6\) {) Tj
T*
(    const x = Waves.wave\(y + t, 'classicSine', null, { amplitude: 80 }\);) Tj
T*
(    point\(width / 2 + x, y\);) Tj
T*
(  }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
(WORKFLOW 2: GRID / WEBGL) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
