BT
/F1 11 Tf
54 738 Td
14 TL
(------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
(1\) Normalize + range Normalize keeps outputs within a consistent range:) Tj
T*
(  const x = Waves.wave\(y, 'classicSine', null, {) Tj
T*
(    normalize: true,) Tj
T*
(    range: [-1, 1]) Tj
T*
(  }\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2\) Domain and samples Domain and samples control internal sampling and normalization:) Tj
T*
(  const x = Waves.wave\(y, 'classicSine', null, {) Tj
T*
(    normalize: true,) Tj
T*
(    domain: [-300, 300],) Tj
T*
(    samples: 512) Tj
T*
(  }\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3\) Auto-advance with seconds Every N seconds, the wave changes based on refresh:) Tj
T*
(  const x = Waves.wave\(y, 'classicSine', 2, { amplitude: 80 }\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4\) Refresh \(deterministic shifts\) Refresh lets you change the phase or pick different waves:) Tj
T*
(  const x = Waves.wave\(y, 'classicSine', null, { refresh: 5 }\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5\) Use a sampler for speed) Tj
T*
(  const sampler = Waves.createSampler\({ axis: 'xz', amplitude: 60 }\);) Tj
T*
(  const o = sampler.sample\(y\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
(TROUBLESHOOTING) Tj
T*
(------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
(- If outputs look too small, increase amplitude. - If outputs explode, reduce amplitude or) Tj
T*
(normalize. - If a name doesn't match, try a different alias or index. - If you want) Tj
T*
(deterministic results across sessions, fix refresh.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
(RECAP) Tj
T*
(------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
(- Use Waves.wave\(\) for simple sampling. - Animate by changing the input. - Use axis='xz' for) Tj
T*
(WEBGL grids and flow fields. - Map outputs to color, rotation, size, or position. - Store) Tj
T*
(wave names \(strings\) in saved projects.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
